In PostgreSQL, pg_hint_plan is not a standard feature; it is an external extension. For it to work, two things must be true:
1. The extension must be installed on the OS.
2. It must be added to the shared_preload_libraries setting in postgresql.conf and the server must be restarted.
If those aren't set, PostgreSQL treats the /*+ ... */ as a regular comment and ignores it completely. This is why your plan remained the same.

 pg_hint_plan

 /*+
      NestedLoop(cc ccd)
      NestedLoop(cc cc_4)
      NestedLoop(cc frc)
      IndexScan(cc)
   */
SELECT * FROM public.humana_claim_report(544,'266390013461','RTL','','','','','N','','N','','');

If it does not work, added into share_library and restart server. 
